# Audio DSP, GPU and video firmware for the Honor MagicBook Art 14. The firmware only runs if it
# is signed for this board by Honor, so linux-firmware cannot carry it until the OEM submits it.
# The OEM ships it in its Windows driver download, which this recipe unpacks without running. Each
# file is checked against the SHA-256 it was matched to and installed under the name the device
# tree requests, compressed with xz. The kernel tries a plain name, then .zst, then .xz, so once
# linux-firmware ships the same file, its copy is the one loaded, and the two packages never
# install the same path.
#
# Generated from https://arewearmyet.com/firmware-sources.json by
# https://github.com/birkskyum/arewearmyet/blob/main/scripts/snapdragon-firmware-recipes.py;
# change the table, not this file.

